      "math_academy_id": "q-112812",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-6{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+4{b}_{1}-6{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2(2{b}_{1})-2(3{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
